    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "body": "> I can reproduce this with v0.13.0-dev-631+ga5d4b4e0fc and `nvim --clean`. I just wanted to create an issue about it. Although not with OP's `autocmd.txt` example, but with e.g. the line that states the default value for `g:netrw_sort_sequence`.\n> \n> Renders:\n> \n> ```\n>                                  default: '[\\/]$,,\\.bak$,\\.o$,\\.h$,\n>                                            \\.info$,\\.swp$,\\.obj$'\n> ```\n> \n> Should be:\n> \n> ```\n>                                  default: '[\\/]$,*,\\.bak$,\\.o$,\\.h$,\n>                                            \\.info$,\\.swp$,\\.obj$'\n> ```\n> \n> Note how in the first example there is no asterisk in the beginning of the first line. \n\n _Originally posted by @camoz in [#29204](https://github.com/neovim/neovim/issues/29204#issuecomment-5941199020)_",
